language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Hidato: fill an n by n board with the numbers 1 to n*n, each once, so that consecutive numbers touch horizontally, vertically or diagonally, and the given clue numbers stay in their cells.
given puzzle_dim1, puzzle_dim2 : int(1..)
$ the board is square, so its side is the number of rows
letting n = puzzle_dim1
$ the clue numbers as given, 0 for an empty cell
given puzzle : matrix indexed by [int(1..puzzle_dim1), int(1..puzzle_dim2)] of int(0..puzzle_dim1*puzzle_dim2)
$ the squares that touch each other (horizontally, vertically or diagonally), each square numbered (row-1)*n+column
letting Touch = [ [(r1-1)*n+c1, (r2-1)*n+c2] | r1 : int(1..n), c1 : int(1..n), r2 : int(1..n), c2 : int(1..n), (|r1-r2| <= 1) /\ (|c1-c2| <= 1) /\ ((r1 != r2) \/ (c1 != c2)) ]
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..n), int(1..n)] of int(1..n*n)
$ row and column of the square holding each number
find rowOf : matrix indexed by [int(1..n*n)] of int(1..n)
find colOf : matrix indexed by [int(1..n*n)] of int(1..n)
$ the square of each number as one index from 1 to n*n
find cell : matrix indexed by [int(1..n*n)] of int(1..n*n)
branching on [cell]
such that
$ every square holds a different number
allDiff(cell),
$ each number k sits in the square given by rowOf and colOf, and x shows it
forAll k : int(1..n*n) . ((cell[k] = (rowOf[k]-1)*n + colOf[k]) /\ (x[rowOf[k], colOf[k]] = k)),
$ a clue number sits in its clue square
forAll r : int(1..n) . forAll c : int(1..n) . (puzzle[r,c] != 0 -> cell[puzzle[r,c]] = (r-1)*n + c),
$ consecutive numbers k and k+1 are in touching squares
forAll k : int(1..n*n-1) . table([cell[k], cell[k+1]], Touch)
